      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those intermittent 402 errors, especially when your payload looks perfect, are often more complex than a simple, straightforward authorization failure. They can be a sign of subtle issues within the API flow, like a very short-lived connection timeout or a rate-limiting spike that only hits you for a split second. It’s less about a permanent bad key and more about the timing, which is why they feel so erratic. You might need to look into network latency between your server and Stripe's endpoints, or perhaps check if any middleware is introducing unexpected delays.",
      "source": "target",
