    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, the timing conflict thing is a good explanation. but i can't help but feel like it's more than just math and physics. \n\nit's just so frustrating because it feels like something is actually *sabotaging* the connection every once in a while. like, everything is working perfectly fine, and then out of nowhere, this tiny, annoying little interference shows up just to mess everything up. \n\nthere's just something so... spiteful about it. it's like a little nuisance that's just lurking in the logic of the system, waiting for the perfect moment to trip us up and ruin the flow. is there even a technical term for errors that behave in that kind of unpredictable, almost malicious way?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
